# ── Environment config: never commit ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The `.env` / `.env.local` entries above match ONLY files named exactly that.
# A prefixed variant does not match, so `prod-api.env` and `prod-web.env` — the
# real production configuration — sat untracked but unignored in the repo root,
# one `git add .` away from being committed and pushed to both remotes (one of
# which is the client's). Match the suffix, not just the exact name.
#
# `.env.example` is deliberately NOT covered: it carries no values and is meant
# to be committed as the documented list of required variables.
